       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Going above that dose adds little blood pressure benefit and raises the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nCan you check whether 20 mg is what you intended? Here are some options:\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, if the patient is new to the drug.\n- **Another agent added to amlodipine.** If 10 mg isn't controlling BP, adding an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred to going above the maximum.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter that."
      }
